{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/trackinganalytics"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"title":"Tracking Screen Analytics"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/TrackingAnalytics"},"abstract":[{"text":"Send screen-opened and state-transition events to any analytics backend with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsService","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsService","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsTracker","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/NoOpScreenAnalyticsTracker"],"title":"Related Documentation"},{"anchor":"Analytics","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsService","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsTracker","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/AnalyticsValue","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/NoOpScreenAnalyticsTracker"],"title":"Analytics"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every screen that models its state with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true},{"text":" already knows exactly when it was opened and when it moves between Empty, Loading, Data, and Error. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsService","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" turns those moments into ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"s and fans them out to as many "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsTracker","type":"reference"},{"text":"s as you register — one per analytics backend (Firebase, Mixpanel, Amplitude, your own logging endpoint, a debug console print, …).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ScreenStates ships no backend-specific tracker implementations, so the core module stays dependency-free — but it does include "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker","isActive":true},{"text":" (logs every event to the console) and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/NoOpScreenAnalyticsTracker","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (silently discards everything), so you don’t have to hand-roll a console logger just to confirm events fire at the right moments. For a real backend, write one small adapter, converting the event’s backend-agnostic "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/AnalyticsValue","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" parameters into that SDK’s own format:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct FirebaseScreenTracker: ScreenAnalyticsTracker {","    func track(_ event: ScreenAnalyticsEvent) {","        Analytics.logEvent(event.name, parameters: event.parameters.mapValues { value in","            switch value {","            case .string(let string): string","            case .int(let int): int","            case .double(let double): double","            case .bool(let bool): bool","            }","        })","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An adapter is also free to remap "},{"code":"event.name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to whatever vocabulary its backend expects — Firebase, for example, reserves a specific constant for screen views."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Wiring-a-screen","text":"Wiring a screen"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let analytics = ScreenAnalyticsService(trackers: [FirebaseScreenTracker(), PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker()])","","func onAppear(source: ScreenOpenSource<AppScreen>) {","    analytics.trackScreenOpened(\"Articles\", source: source.analyticsKind)","    analytics.observeStateChanges(of: store, screen: \"Articles\")","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackScreenOpened(_:source:)"},{"text":" sends one ","type":"text"},{"code":"screen_opened","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" event. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"observeStateChanges(of:screen:)"},{"type":"text","text":" uses the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withObservationTracking"},{"type":"text","text":" mechanism "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView"},{"type":"text","text":" uses to mirror a store, and sends a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_state_changed"},{"type":"text","text":" event for every subsequent "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"type":"text","text":" transition — call it once, right where you create or first observe the store. When a transition lands on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":", the event also carries the error’s "},{"code":"localizedDescription","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It also times how long the screen spends in ","type":"text"},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the moment the state leaves "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":", it sends a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_load_duration"},{"type":"text","text":" event ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenLoadDuration(screen:outcome:milliseconds:)"},{"type":"text","text":") with that outcome and the elapsed time in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duration_ms"},{"type":"text","text":" — useful for a “how long do loads actually take, and how often do they end in an error” dashboard without hand-rolling a stopwatch around every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" call."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_state_changed"},{"text":" event landing on ","type":"text"},{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tells you a screen failed to load; it doesn’t tell you whether the user gave up or hit Retry. Call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackRetryTapped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","identif